  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1102 AM MST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nDRIER CONDITIONS FOR SUNDAY & MONDAY:\n\nThere is potential for fog and low stratus once again tonight.\nThe only difference is that clouds moving in form the west could\nprohibit some of that development. \n\nNEXT SYSTEM TUESDAY-WEDNESDAY:\n\nOur focus then shifts to another shortwave trough moving through the \narea from Tuesday afternoon through Wednesday. While this system \nwill be slightly cooler, the bulk of the precipitation is still \nexpected to fall ahead of the cold front. As a result, snowfall \ntotals should look similar to the previous system, peaking at 4-8\" \nin the southern mountains, with lighter amounts farther north. Snow \nlevels will also be hovering around 7-9 kft. Behind the front, \ntemperatures will drop to near or slightly below normal for much of \nthe week. \n\nLATE WEEK SYSTEM: \n\nForecast models continue to show another system arriving late this \nweek on Friday and Saturday. Models still show an open wave \nsetup, so as a result the precipitation amounts continue to\ndecrease. There is still some differences among the models with\nregards to strength and timing, so confidence is not high attm.\nMost of the moisture is expected to arrive ahead of the cold \nfront, making timing critical. Snow levels could drop to some \nvalley floors Friday night into Saturday morning. For now, \nhowever, the specifics remain uncertain.",
